The 35 Type 1 font programs this crate embeds (../stet/resources/Font/*.t1,
embedded from the stet crate) are the
URW++ base 35 fonts. Their own notices read "Copyright 2013 by (URW)++
Design & Development" (one font), "Copyright 2014 by (URW)++ Design &
Development" (33 fonts), and "Copyright 2015 by URW" (one font).

They are not covered by this crate's Apache-2.0 OR MIT licence. stet
distributes them under the SIL Open Font License, Version 1.1.

The grant
---------

URW++ offers these fonts under a choice of three licences: the GNU Affero
General Public License v3 with a font exception, the LaTeX Project Public
License 1.3c, and the SIL Open Font License 1.1. stet takes the OFL.

URW++'s managing director, Peter Rosenfeld, approved adding the OFL on
26 February 2016. In May 2017 URW++'s technical director, Juergen
Willrodt, gave Adam Twardoch administrator access to URW++'s GitHub
organisation (URWPP, later renamed URWTypeFoundry), and on 2 September
2017 Twardoch committed the three licences to URW++'s Core_35 repository.
Twardoch records this authorisation, with its dates, in his archive of
the fonts:

  https://github.com/twardoch/urw-core35-fonts/blob/cb9f45f7a4f83a97d959710f0c9f8020e46bdd14/docs/provenance.md

URW++'s repository is no longer online; Twardoch reports that it was
closed after Monotype acquired URW Type Foundry. An archived copy shows
the three licences in URW++'s own repository, at commit 1b5267a:

  https://web.archive.org/web/20200904172916/https://github.com/URWTypeFoundry/Core_35/

and Twardoch's archive keeps that commit:

  https://github.com/twardoch/urw-core35-fonts/tree/1b5267a9a14d8d5bcf261e067187e382df40c520

The files
---------

The files here are URW++'s 2017 revisions of its Version 2.0 set (the
2017-05-01, 2017-07-20 and 2017-07-27 updates) and a 2020 correction to
Nimbus Sans Italic and Bold Italic. They are byte-identical to the Type 1
files in Twardoch's archive at the revision above (tag v2.2.0), which
offers them under the same three licences, and to the Type 1 files in
https://github.com/ArtifexSoftware/urw-base35-fonts (fonts/*.t1).

URW++ supplied these revisions to Artifex, whose repository publishes
them under the AGPL option alone; the OFL and LPPL choices come from
URW++'s authorisation above, not from Artifex. Rosenfeld's approval
predates the June 2016 release of Version 2.0, so it was given for the
font set rather than for one release of its files. Artifex's commit of
the 2020 correction credits URW++ as its source:

  https://github.com/ArtifexSoftware/urw-base35-fonts/commit/c15105598aa7eb256b1ebfcecd3d078801521e73

Reproduced below from URW++'s repository at commit 1b5267a: its
LICENSE.md, followed by its LICENSE.OFL (line endings converted from CRLF
to LF).

